<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
      DB-GENERATED UUID PRIMARY KEYS — the owncast-BFF migration (exemplars: merged
      mod-bff #36, changelog 009-mod-action-db-generated-id.xml; admin-bff #133,
      changelog 200-db-generated-uuid-pks.xml).

      Decision (pinned): stop minting UUID primary keys in Java
      (UUID.randomUUID().toString()); let Postgres generate them via a column DEFAULT and
      read the generated id back on insert (INSERT ... RETURNING id). The column type and
      the entity @Id type are UNCHANGED — only the SOURCE of the id moves from the app to
      the database.

      All three owncast-BFF PK tables carry a varchar id string PK that was minted in Java
      as UUID.randomUUID().toString(). For a varchar id the DB default casts the native
      uuid to text — (gen_random_uuid())::text — which yields the lowercase 36-char
      hyphenated form, BYTE-IDENTICAL to UUID.randomUUID().toString() (and well within the
      varchar(64) column width). The column type + the entity @Id type stay String; only
      the id SOURCE moves to the DB. Each repository INSERT omits id and RETURNING id reads
      the generated string back (the deterministic, mod-bff-proven path).

      ── tables ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        owncast_grant            (004) — varchar(64) id; was OwncastGrantRepository.insertActive()
        owncast_stream           (005) — varchar(64) id; was OwncastStreamRepository.insert()
        owncast_moderation_audit (006) — varchar(64) id; was OwncastModerationAuditRepository.insert()

      Numbered 007 — one band above the current max (006). Registered LAST in
      db.changelog-master.xml.

      The H2 PostgreSQL-compat slice store (TestDatabaseConfig) has neither pgcrypto nor a
      reliable INSERT ... RETURNING, so the prod changelog can no longer be applied over it.
      That is exactly why the affected @DataR2dbcTest slices move to the commons
      Testcontainers-Postgres base (PostgresTestSupport) — mirroring mod-bff #36 — so
      gen_random_uuid() and RETURNING run for real against the same engine as production.
    -->

    <!-- FIRST: ensure gen_random_uuid() is available. Built-in on PG13+, but install
         pgcrypto defensively (idempotent + harmless if already present) — mirrors the
         mod-bff / admin-bff exemplars' pgcrypto changeSet. Gated to PostgreSQL with a
         dbms precondition (this repo gates its PG-only changeSets the same way — see
         004-owncast-grant-active-unique): the test store IS Postgres and the production
         runtime is Postgres. -->
    <changeSet id="007-pgcrypto-extension" author="hugmesh">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN" onError="MARK_RAN">
            <dbms type="postgresql"/>
        </preConditions>
        <comment>Install pgcrypto so gen_random_uuid() is available as the
                 DB-generated-UUID column DEFAULT. IF NOT EXISTS — idempotent.</comment>
        <sql>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pgcrypto;</sql>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- owncast_grant.id (varchar(64), changelog 004): DB-generate via
         (gen_random_uuid())::text instead of OwncastGrantRepository minting
         UUID.randomUUID().toString(). The column stays varchar PK; the repository INSERT
         omits id and RETURNING id reads the generated string back. -->
    <changeSet id="007-gen-uuid-owncast_grant" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>DB-generate owncast_grant.id ((gen_random_uuid())::text) instead of the
                 app minting it; INSERT omits id, RETURNING id reads it back.</comment>
        <addDefaultValue tableName="owncast_grant"
                         columnName="id"
                         columnDataType="varchar(64)"
                         defaultValueComputed="(gen_random_uuid())::text"/>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- owncast_stream.id (varchar(64), changelog 005): DB-generate via
         (gen_random_uuid())::text instead of OwncastStreamRepository minting
         UUID.randomUUID().toString(). -->
    <changeSet id="007-gen-uuid-owncast_stream" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>DB-generate owncast_stream.id ((gen_random_uuid())::text) instead of the
                 app minting it; INSERT omits id, RETURNING id reads it back.</comment>
        <addDefaultValue tableName="owncast_stream"
                         columnName="id"
                         columnDataType="varchar(64)"
                         defaultValueComputed="(gen_random_uuid())::text"/>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- owncast_moderation_audit.id (varchar(64), changelog 006): DB-generate via
         (gen_random_uuid())::text instead of OwncastModerationAuditRepository minting
         UUID.randomUUID().toString(). -->
    <changeSet id="007-gen-uuid-owncast_moderation_audit" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>DB-generate owncast_moderation_audit.id ((gen_random_uuid())::text) instead
                 of the app minting it; INSERT omits id, RETURNING id reads it back.</comment>
        <addDefaultValue tableName="owncast_moderation_audit"
                         columnName="id"
                         columnDataType="varchar(64)"
                         defaultValueComputed="(gen_random_uuid())::text"/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
